      "message": "\u003e Now we also can\u0027t just check if riscv64 is present in SUPPORTED_ABIS, because that could also trigger false positives (because berberis).\n\nlike i said, my assumption is that that doesn\u0027t work? i\u0027ve asked levarum to comment though --- he\u0027ll know[1]. (because, yes, if that works, this is the right code.)\n\n(that is: my suggestion is literally \"if the list contains riscv64, throw\".)\n\n____\n1. at least from the _berberis_ side --- i\u0027d still assume someone would have to do work on the renderscript side to have renderscript generate code _not_ for the native architecture, if the native architecture is riscv64. i can guarantee _that_ code doesn\u0027t currently exist, unless you have another patch pending :-)",
