      "writtenOn": "2024-02-16T01:37:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For berberis we have disabled guest renderscript libraries [1] because we couldn\u0027t even build them. Berberis will not make riscv64 apps use host (x86/arm) renderscript. Such apps will crash.\n\nOTOH, I\u0027m not sure we want to break x86 apps on systems with berberis by saying that \"renderscript is not supported since there is riscv64 *in addition* to x86_64\".\n\nIdeally, we should only throw here if the app is launched as riscv64. Unfortunately I don\u0027t know an easy way to tell this from here.\n\nI\u0027m thinking the most general way to detect unsupported situation is when attempting to load `libRS.so` or `libRSDriver.so` in app\u0027s loader namespace since iiuc they won\u0027t exist for riscv64.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/libs/native_bridge_support/native_bridge_support.mk;l\u003d108;drc\u003d6da5256fdae204110bb948556194af885a16a9f9",
      "parentUuid": "2925c150_461eeb69",
